WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.840
Every image starts as a link.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.200
One is easy.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.510
Three thousand is a different question.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.100
You start with a list.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.270
Every row becomes a job.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.470
How fast?

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.180
Machyon measures.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.740
It adds connections while speed improves,

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.290
and steps back when it doesn't.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.950
Sometimes, a server asks you to slow down.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.170
The others keep going.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.180
The server says everything's fine.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.100
Machyon checks anyway.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.350
A file gets its name only when it's complete.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.410
So stopping is safe.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.180
Start a run.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.390
Stop it partway.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.100
Resume, and it only fetches what's missing.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.080
Every row is accounted for.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.470
Even failures come with a reason.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.720
One link, then three thousand.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.370
Every one answered.

